# The offset columns, the hex tables and the comment blocks in this folder are
# laid out by hand and carry meaning - an aligned /* 0x… */ column is how every
# line is checked against the disassembly. No formatter reproduces that: the
# closest clang-format config still rewrites 4,163 lines of it.
#
# So: leave it alone. This file is what tells clangd, conform.nvim, VS Code and
# anything else clang-format-based to keep its hands off, whatever the editor is
# configured to do.
DisableFormat: true
SortIncludes: Never
